From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Clay Stan <claystan97@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 24 Nov 2026 12:13:00 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] drm/panthor: retry a deferred performance-domain attachment

A named performance domain can exist before its SCMI provider registers.
The attachment helper returns -EPROBE_DEFER in that case, but the SCMI
OPP setup currently treats every error as an absent optional domain.
On ACPI this falls through to the DT OPP lookup and returns -ENODEV,
preventing the GPU from being retried after the provider becomes ready.

Preserve -EPROBE_DEFER so panthor_devfreq_init() propagates it to probe.
Keep the existing fallback for other results, including -EEXIST when a
non-ACPI device already has its primary domain attached.

Signed-off-by: Clay Stan <claystan97@gmail.com>
---
 drivers/gpu/drm/panthor/panthor_devfreq.c | 3 +++
 1 file changed, 3 insertions(+)

diff --git a/drivers/gpu/drm/panthor/panthor_devfreq.c b/drivers/gpu/drm/panthor/panthor_devfreq.c
--- a/drivers/gpu/drm/panthor/panthor_devfreq.c
+++ b/drivers/gpu/drm/panthor/panthor_devfreq.c
@@ -207,6 +207,9 @@
 	 * would do).
 	 */
 	opp_dev = dev_pm_domain_attach_by_name(dev, "perf");
+	/* Retry when firmware describes a perf domain whose provider is not ready. */
+	if (IS_ERR(opp_dev) && PTR_ERR(opp_dev) == -EPROBE_DEFER)
+		return -EPROBE_DEFER;
 	if (IS_ERR_OR_NULL(opp_dev))
 		return 0;
 
